            0.393
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6.4 Nature’s Favourite Sequence: The Virahāṅka– Fibonacci Numbers!"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.404,
            0.848,
            0.515
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The sequence 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13, 21, 34, . . . ("
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Virahāṅka–Fibonacci Numbers",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ") is one of the most celebrated sequences in all of mathematics — it occurs throughout the world of Art, Science, and Mathematics. Even though these numbers are found very frequently in Science, it is remarkable that these numbers were first discovered in the context of Art (specifically, poetry)!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.514,
            0.846,
            0.553
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Virahāṅka–Fibonacci Numbers",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " thus provide a beautiful illustration of the close links between Art, Science, and Mathematics."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.571,
            0.609,
            0.592
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Discovery of the Virahāṅka Numbers"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.602,
            0.846,
            0.64
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The Virahāṅka numbers first came up thousands of years ago in the works of Sanskrit and Prakrit linguists in their study of poetry!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.64,
            0.847,
            0.695
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In the poetry of many Indian languages, including, Prakrit, Sanskrit, Marathi, Malayalam, Tamil, and Telugu, each syllable is classified as either long or short."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.695,
            0.848,
            0.768
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A long syllable is pronounced for a longer duration than a short syllable — in fact, for exactly twice as long. When singing such a poem, a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "short syllable",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " lasts one beat of time, and a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "long syllable",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " lasts two beats of time."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.768,
            0.848,
            0.842
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This leads to numerous mathematical questions, which the ancient poets in these languages considered extensively. A number of important mathematical discoveries were made in the process of asking and answering these questions about poetry."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.842,
            0.817,
            0.86
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "One of these particularly important questions was the following."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.86,
            0.848,
            0.898
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How many rhythms are there with 8 beats consisting of short syllables (1 beat) and long syllables (2 beats)? That is, in how many ways can one"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.806,
            0.938,
            0.846,
            0.955
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "139"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 15,
